# The PDA writing zone (report 041) as the text input of a native page: Settings > System > Keyboard test (development
# channel), its Text field written with pen strokes through the touch path, the router and the recogniser with the
# shipped tables (no on-screen keyboard: vkb=zone). The strokes are the shipped templates drawn about 12 mm high in the
# boxes (points in px from the box's corner). Shots: the mode line after the shift gesture ("Abc", Shift), after the
# extended prefix (Ext), the field with "Lit £1" (a pound sign through the extended set: no US key, typed as text alone;
# the field's builtin font has no glyph for it, the text is checked), and a stroke in progress (its ink).
# Goldens at both sizes.
title zone text
sizes 480x640 480x800
profile pda
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 1
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
launch Settings
key UP
key ENTER
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
expect_vkb zone
stroke letters 60,130 60,30
shot zone_text_shift
stroke letters 60,30 60,130 121,130
stroke letters 60,30 60,130
stroke letters 60,30 118,30 121,130
stroke letters 40,80 140,80
stroke letters 60,30 145,115
shot zone_text_ext
stroke letters 60,30 60,130 121,130
stroke digits 50,30 50,130
expect_text "Lit £1"
shot zone_text
stroke letters 120,30 120,90 hold
shot zone_ink
release
expect_text "Lit £1i"
